# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build-context filter for the repo root.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: every deployable image in this repository — web/Dockerfile
# (app.stonkhouse.fun), keeper/Dockerfile (the weekly roll), indexer/Dockerfile (Ponder and the
# /v1 read API) and relay/Dockerfile (keeper alerts → Discord/Telegram) — is built with the
# REPO ROOT as the build context, because pnpm-lock.yaml and pnpm-workspace.yaml live here and
# the install has to be workspace-aware. Without this file the daemon uploads node_modules,
# every .next cache and the contracts/ submodule (with its own Foundry submodules) on every
# deploy — hundreds of megabytes, to produce the same image. The landing (stonkhouse.fun) builds
# from its own repository, stonkhousedotfun/callhouse-site, since the 2026-09-13 split.
#
# WHAT MUST STAY IN, and why:
#   package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml  — the workspace install reads all three.
#   <pkg>/package.json for EVERY workspace member      — `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` compares
#     the lockfile's importer set against the workspace. Drop keeper/package.json and the install
#     fails with "lockfile is not up to date", even though not one line of keeper code reaches the
#     web image. That is the only reason for the `dir/*` + `!dir/package.json` pairs below.
#   keeper/tsconfig.json, keeper/src                   — keeper/Dockerfile COPYs both; it is the
#     one image that ships keeper code. keeper/src also rides into the web context
#     unread — a few hundred kilobytes, and cheaper than per-image context files.
#   indexer/{abis,lib,src,ponder.*.ts,tsconfig.json}   — indexer/Dockerfile COPYs these; Ponder
#     loads the TypeScript sources at boot, so they are the whole of the indexer image.
#   relay/tsconfig.json, relay/src                     — relay/Dockerfile COPYs both.
#   scripts/                                           — small, and package scripts reach for it
#     (`web/package.json` → `node ../scripts/copy-lint.mjs`).
#
# keeper/.dockerignore exists too but is INERT: Docker reads only the context-root file, and
# the keeper's context root is the repo root. It is kept for its list of keeper-local runtime
# artifacts; this file is the one that decides.
#
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT: any exception that lets a `.env` file into a context. Nothing in .env* may
# ever enter an image. Build-time values arrive as ARGs from Railway (see the Dockerfiles) and
# runtime values as Railway service variables.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- never in any image ----
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/.pnpm-store
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitmodules
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
HANDOFF.md
.codex
.claude
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
lcov.info

# ---- secrets. No exception line may follow this block. ----
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# ---- Solidity. Source, artefacts and the Foundry submodules (contracts/lib is the big one).
#      `next build` reads none of it: web/lib/abi/*.ts are generated and committed. ----
contracts
broadcast

# ---- ops and docs. ops/abis is the source of truth for the ABIs, but generation is a manual
#      `pnpm gen:abis`, never part of `next build`. ----
ops
# … except the market registry: the v2 bots read it at boot (keeper/Dockerfile runner stage,
# ops/deploy.md §15.2).
!ops/markets/tier1.json
# … and the v2 external monitor, which the keeper image runs as the `monitor` service (ops/deploy.md §15.12).
!ops/v2/monitor.mjs
# Next type-checks web/lib/v2/config.test.ts during `next build`, and that file statically imports
# this JSON fixture. Keep the single fixture in the web build context; the runner copies only
# standalone output, so it is not shipped in the runtime image.
!ops/fixtures/api/v2/config.json
docs
plan.md
tasks.md
TECHSPEC.md
SECURITY.md

# ---- workspace packages that never belong in a web image, except their manifest. Removing the
#      manifest breaks the frozen install — see the header. Each package then re-admits exactly
#      the paths its own Dockerfile COPYs; without them that build fails at the COPY. Tests,
#      READMEs, the indexer's vitest config and scripts/gen-abis.mjs stay out. ----
keeper/*
!keeper/package.json
!keeper/tsconfig.json
!keeper/src
# Rights review hold: these local, Git-ignored files must not enter a Docker
# build context either (including builds run from this dirty worktree).
keeper/src/fixtures/cboe-tsla-2026-09-16.json
keeper/src/v2/pricing/cboe.test.ts
keeper/src/v2/pricing/surface.test.ts
keeper/src/v2/pricing/fair.test.ts
indexer/*
!indexer/package.json
!indexer/tsconfig.json
!indexer/ponder.config.ts
!indexer/ponder.schema.ts
!indexer/ponder-env.d.ts
!indexer/abis
!indexer/lib
!indexer/src
relay/*
!relay/package.json
!relay/tsconfig.json
!relay/src

# ---- runtime state that can exist locally ----
**/.ponder
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.sqlite
